Package: ndopred
Title: Automated IUCN Red List Assessment for NDOP Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jonáš", "Gaigr", , "jonas.gaigr@aopk.gov.cz", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Automates the calculation of IUCN Red List metrics using occurrence
    data from the NDOP database. It includes functions to calculate Extent of
    Occurrence (EOO), Area of Occupancy (AOO), population trends (Criterion A),
    and population size metrics (Criteria C/D). Thresholds follow the IUCN Red
    List Categories and Criteria v3.1 (2012) and their interpretation follows
    the Guidelines for Using the IUCN Red List Categories and Criteria v16
    (2024), including logic for Near Threatened (NT) and Data Deficient (DD)
    statuses. Judgements that occurrence records cannot supply - severe
    fragmentation, habitat decline, and the plausible threat required by
    criterion D2 - are left to the assessor rather than inferred. Includes
    interactive Shiny dashboards for bulk screening and for expert
    verification with manual overrides.
